From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 12:38:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] nvme-apple: Take T8132 ANS through a firmware-driven
 sleep

The firmware-driven suspend path registers only controllers whose sleep
has been traced, which so far is T8140's. On T8132 apple-s2r now drives
suspend-to-RAM, ANS loses its power there like on T8140, and without
its stop and warm restart the disk would not come back.

Register T8132's ANS with the same path, under a separate flag so that
nothing claims a trace that hasn't happened, and with no value taken
from T8140:

- The shutdown notification is the specification's normal shutdown,
  which this driver already sends on post-M4 controllers at the final
  system shutdown. T8140's is the value read back from macOS there.
- The warm restart echoes the whole endpoint map, RTKit's default,
  instead of T8140's endpoint 0x20 alone.
- Only namespace 1 is flushed, the one Linux mounts.

The path only runs when apple-s2r has begun a suspend-to-RAM, which
needs apple_s2r.enable=1 and a warm boot mailbox from m1n1; s2idle is
unchanged. Whether ANS accepts the notification, what its endpoint map
looks like after the restart, and which namespaces are the firmware's
are measured in the first dev-loop runs.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
(cherry picked from commit 8152063ef18a01428ff2432b1057595b0a0b3e16)
(cherry picked from commit ca921a8a3dd0807f6d35010baa1d09e22a152710)
---
 drivers/nvme/host/apple.c | 17 ++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/nvme/host/apple.c b/drivers/nvme/host/apple.c
index a5124a299e..c592bb2644 100644
--- a/drivers/nvme/host/apple.c
+++ b/drivers/nvme/host/apple.c
@@ -216,6 +216,11 @@ struct apple_nvme_hw {
 	bool cold_reset;
 	/* Firmware-driven suspend has been traced on this controller. */
 	bool sleep_traced;
+	/*
+	 * Not traced: the same path with values that come from no other SoC, for the
+	 * dev loop that measures them (TO-VERIFY until it has).
+	 */
+	bool sleep_probe;
 	/* The last endpoint map reply from that trace */
 	u32 sleep_epmap_last_mask;
 	/* Higher namespaces are the firmware's, and a Flush to one faults the controller. */
@@ -2674,7 +2679,7 @@ static int apple_nvme_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 
 	INIT_DELAYED_WORK(&anv->flush_dwork, apple_nvme_flush_work);
 
-	if (anv->hw->sleep_traced) {
+	if (anv->hw->sleep_traced || anv->hw->sleep_probe) {
 		anv->sleep_registered =
 			!apple_sleep_coproc_register(anv->dev, anv->mmio_coproc, true,
 						     apple_nvme_sleep_last_stop, anv);
@@ -3026,6 +3031,16 @@ static const struct apple_nvme_hw apple_nvme_t8132_hw = {
 	.max_queue_depth = 64,
 	/* Explicit flushes are required for writes to survive a reset on J713. */
 	.quirks = NVME_QUIRK_BROKEN_FUA,
+	/*
+	 * Only in a suspend-to-RAM that apple-s2r drives (pm_suspend_via_firmware());
+	 * s2idle is unchanged. SHN: the spec's normal shutdown, as this driver sends at
+	 * final shutdown. Warm restart: the whole endpoint map echoed, RTKit's default.
+	 * Flush: namespace 1, the one Linux mounts. All three are to be measured.
+	 */
+	.sleep_probe = true,
+	.sleep_epmap_last_mask = U32_MAX,
+	.sleep_flush_max_nsid = 1,
+	.sleep_shn = NVME_CC_SHN_NORMAL,
 };
 
 static const struct apple_nvme_hw apple_nvme_t8140_hw = {
